# Direct dependencies of the Goal 1 / CPU-analysis environment ($PY).
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS.  env/requirements-goal1.txt is a raw `pip freeze` of the
# original box's venv and is NOT installable as-is: it pins vllm==0.5.5 and
# torch==2.4.0 but ALSO torchaudio==2.11.0 (needs torch 2.11), opencv-python-headless
# 4.13 (needs numpy>=2, while numpy==1.26.4 is pinned), flashinfer 0.6.8,
# xgrammar 0.2.1, mistral_common 1.11 ... i.e. orphans left behind when a newer vLLM
# was replaced by 0.5.5. Pip never removes those and does not check a live env for
# consistency, so the original venv worked; a strict `pip install -r` cannot resolve.
#
# So: install only what src/ actually imports (found by walking the imports of every
# module under src/), and use the freeze purely as CONSTRAINTS. A constraint pins the
# version of anything that gets installed and is ignored for anything that does not,
# so every package the code really needs lands at the original box's version and the
# orphans are simply never installed.
#
#   pip install -r env/requirements-goal1.in -c env/requirements-goal1.txt
#
# Versions are the freeze's. `easysteer` is NOT here: it lives only in the Goal 2 env.
vllm==0.5.5
torch==2.4.0
transformers==4.57.6
numpy==1.26.4
pandas==2.3.3
scipy==1.15.3
scikit-learn==1.7.2
matplotlib==3.10.8
seaborn==0.13.2
pyarrow==23.0.1
# Not imported by anything in src/, but transformers' `device_map=` (used by
# verify_capture.py --stage hf) raises without it. Found by the smoke test.
accelerate==1.13.0
datasets==4.8.4
math-verify==0.9.0
tqdm==4.67.3
